<title>UK: EIB prices 3.0 bln French franc euro-fungible bond.</title>
<headline>EIB prices 3.0 bln French franc euro-fungible bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond, announced earlier by lead manager Banque Nationale de Paris, has now been priced.</p>
<p> BORROWER   EUROPEAN INVESTMENT BANK</p>
<p> AMT    3.0 BLN FFR   COUPON     5.75	MATURITY    15.FEB.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  102.94    PAY DATE  S-10.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.325     REOFFER    102.94    SPREAD	+5 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    PAR LUX   GOV LAW     LUX</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 10-100-1M SALE LIMITS US/UK</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND INTERPOLATED OAT 6.50 PCT DUE OCTOBER 2006</p>
<p>			    AND OAT 5.50 PCT DUE APRIL 2007</p>
<p> NOTES   S SHORT FIRST COUPON</p>
<p>HAS EURO-FUNGIBLE CLAUSE WHICH ALLOWS REDENOMINATION INTO EUROS AFTER THE THIRD STAGE OF EMU. CAN BE CONSOLIDATED WITH 1.0 BLN GUILDER 5.75 PCT 15.FEB.07 BOND AND WITH FUTURE ISSUES WITH IDENTICAL TERMS.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
